{"vid":"tjaLn7URdlA","source":"tjaLn7URdlA.en-GB.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0,"txt":"Do you worry that people can't understand your English?"},{"t":4.2,"txt":"Do you feel nervous when it's your turn to speak?"},{"t":8.5,"txt":"Do you want to sound more like this?"},{"t":11.6,"txt":"I'm going to make a cup of tea. Do you want one?"},{"t":14,"txt":"There's a technique called 'shadowing' that can help you with this."},{"t":18.1,"txt":"In this video, I'll show you exactly how it works and how to use it."},{"t":24.5,"txt":"I think I might have mentioned it."},{"t":26.6,"txt":"This is Lillia."},{"t":28.7,"txt":"She's shadowing a video from our series Pronunciation Shadowing."},{"t":33.6,"txt":"Or she was trying to until I interrupted her. Sorry."},{"t":40.2,"txt":"Shadowing involves listening to a fluent speaker"},{"t":43.9,"txt":"and repeating what they say almost at the same time."},{"t":48,"txt":"This helps train your pronunciation, fluency,"},{"t":52.1,"txt":"and listening all at the same time."},{"t":55.2,"txt":"It particularly helps your rhythm and intonation."},{"t":59.3,"txt":"So now we know why shadowing is useful, but how do you actually do it?"},{"t":68.4,"txt":"First, you need to choose the right audio or video for you."},{"t":72.9,"txt":"Short clips work best with clear intonation and natural pacing."},{"t":77.2,"txt":"You can shadow anything, a conversation or someone just speaking on their own,"},{"t":82.3,"txt":"but it's good if the topic is interesting or useful to you."},{"t":87.7,"txt":"Fortunately, you can find lots of interesting and useful videos"},{"t":91.7,"txt":"and podcasts to shadow on our website, www.bbclearningenglish.com"},{"t":98.6,"txt":"So now that you've got your audio, it's time to shadow."},{"t":103.6,"txt":"You need to find a quiet space to practice in"},{"t":106.9,"txt":"and make sure you have a good pair of headphones."},{"t":111.3,"txt":"The best thing to do now is to practice with short sections and repeat them."},{"t":116.6,"txt":"Here are four simple steps you can follow for effective shadowing."},{"t":125.4,"txt":"Step one: listen without speaking."},{"t":128.8,"txt":"Listen carefully to the intonation and the rhythm of the speech,"},{"t":133.1,"txt":"just like you're listening to a song."},{"t":136.1,"txt":"Step two: listen again and read along with the text."},{"t":141.7,"txt":"I think I might have mentioned it."},{"t":144.2,"txt":"Step three: repeat with a short delay."},{"t":149,"txt":"Try not to look at the text, but keep it near you just in case."},{"t":154.1,"txt":"I think I might have mentioned it."},{"t":156.9,"txt":"Step four: try to shadow with your eyes closed."},{"t":162,"txt":"I think I might have mentioned it."},{"t":164.2,"txt":"And if you need to just pause, rewind and play the same part again."},{"t":170.3,"txt":"When shadowing,"},{"t":171.4,"txt":"it's good to focus on certain pronunciation features."},{"t":175.7,"txt":"You could be trying to improve your pronunciation of 'and'"},{"t":179.4,"txt":"or 'to' in sentences."},{"t":181.4,"txt":"Or maybe you're listening for silent letters."},{"t":184.7,"txt":"Our series Pronunciation Shadowing is perfect for this."},{"t":189.2,"txt":"In this series, a BBC Learning English presenter will read a short paragraph"},{"t":195,"txt":"and give you tips on a specific pronunciation feature in the text."},{"t":199.9,"txt":"For example, Becca helps you with the pronunciation of 'would you'"},{"t":204.6,"txt":"in this episode."},{"t":206.7,"txt":"Would you? Would you like any milk or sugar?"},{"t":213,"txt":"Shadowing will take time and practice,"},{"t":216.3,"txt":"so it's good to motivate yourself by measuring your progress."},{"t":221.1,"txt":"Record yourself reading the text for the first time."},{"t":225.2,"txt":"I think I might have mentioned it."},{"t":228.7,"txt":"It might feel a bit weird at first, but that's normal"},{"t":232.7,"txt":"and you'll soon get used to it. When you've had lots of practice,"},{"t":236.9,"txt":"record yourself again at step four,"},{"t":239.4,"txt":"where you're shadowing without the transcript."},{"t":242.4,"txt":"I think I might have mentioned it."},{"t":244.6,"txt":"Try not to criticise yourself too much"},{"t":247.1,"txt":"and think about the small areas that you've improved in."},{"t":251,"txt":"You might have linked two words together,"},{"t":253.8,"txt":"corrected your pronunciation of a certain word,"},{"t":256.7,"txt":"or your intonation might sound more natural in places."},{"t":260.9,"txt":"So you've learned why shadowing is useful,"},{"t":264.3,"txt":"some tips on how to do it and how to measure your progress."},{"t":269.2,"txt":"Now it's time to do it yourself."},{"t":272.5,"txt":"We have an entire series designed to help"},{"t":275.6,"txt":"with this called Pronunciation Shadowing."},{"t":278.9,"txt":"There are stories, dialogues,"},{"t":281.1,"txt":"and tips for you to shadow with pronunciation features to focus on."},{"t":286.3,"txt":"Click here to watch our shadowing series pronunciation shadowing"},{"t":291.5,"txt":"and click here to see our other pronunciation content."},{"t":296.7,"txt":"Have you tried shadowing before?"},{"t":299,"txt":"Do you have any advice?"},{"t":300.6,"txt":"Write a comment below."}],"words":[{"t":0,"w":"Do"},{"t":0,"w":"you"},{"t":0,"w":"worry"},{"t":0,"w":"that"},{"t":0,"w":"people"},{"t":0,"w":"can't"},{"t":0,"w":"understand"},{"t":0,"w":"your"},{"t":0,"w":"English?"},{"t":4.213,"w":"Do"},{"t":4.213,"w":"you"},{"t":4.213,"w":"feel"},{"t":4.213,"w":"nervous"},{"t":4.213,"w":"when"},{"t":4.213,"w":"it's"},{"t":4.213,"w":"your"},{"t":4.213,"w":"turn"},{"t":4.213,"w":"to"},{"t":4.213,"w":"speak?"},{"t":8.508,"w":"Do"},{"t":8.508,"w":"you"},{"t":8.508,"w":"want"},{"t":8.508,"w":"to"},{"t":8.508,"w":"sound"},{"t":8.508,"w":"more"},{"t":8.508,"w":"like"},{"t":8.508,"w":"this?"},{"t":11.553,"w":"I'm"},{"t":11.553,"w":"going"},{"t":11.553,"w":"to"},{"t":11.553,"w":"make"},{"t":11.553,"w":"a"},{"t":11.553,"w":"cup"},{"t":11.